            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Only for Genuinely Exceptional Circumstances</h4><p>If a genuine, unforeseen event (serious illness, flight cancellation due to force majeure, an urgent unavoidable professional reason) arises after you have entered Germany, apply at your local Ausländerbehörde before your current stay expires, with documentary evidence (e.g. medical certificate, airline cancellation notice).</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>If You Simply Want to Stay Longer</h4><p>There is no extension route for this — plan your trip within the standard 90-day Schengen allowance and apply for a fresh visa for any future visit.</p><p>Our consultants can help you understand whether your specific circumstances could qualify as an exceptional reason before you approach the Ausländerbehörde.</p>',
